<crash-analysis>
The crash is caused by a stack-buffer-overflow in the `pcap_findalldevs_ex` function in `pcap.c`. The variable `stringlen` is 0, and the code attempts to access `name[stringlen - 1]`, which results in reading from `name[-1]`, causing a one-byte underflow.

The fix is to add a check to ensure `stringlen` is greater than 0 before attempting to access `name[stringlen - 1]`.

```c
if (stringlen > 0 && name[stringlen - 1] != ENDING_CHAR) {
```
</crash-analysis>

